WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.375
Lesson 6.5.

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:05.205
Case studies: how DeFi failures happened.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.056
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:09.070
be able to learn the patterns behind

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.410
major failures so you recognise them early.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.000
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.685
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.685 --> 00:00:18.400
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.925
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:22.087
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:26.462
Figures are approximate, from public reporting.

00:00:26.462 --> 00:00:31.123
Black Thursday, March 2020 (Maker), ETH crashed; congested

00:00:31.123 --> 00:00:35.231
network and failing keeper bots let some collateral

00:00:35.231 --> 00:00:38.548
auctions clear at 0 DAI bids (~$8M lost),

00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:43.604
Liquidation mechanism failure under stress, Auctions relying on

00:00:43.604 --> 00:00:47.222
keepers during congestion; no minimum bid.

00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:51.965
TerraUSD (UST), May 2022, Algorithmic stablecoin lost its

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:56.544
peg and collapsed, Reflexive design: confidence was the

00:00:56.544 --> 00:01:00.551
collateral, Yield (~20%) far above any real cash

00:01:00.551 --> 00:01:03.877
flow; peg defended by a sister token.

00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:08.283
Ronin bridge, March 2022 (~$600M), Attackers got

00:01:08.283 --> 00:01:11.431
5 of 9 validator keys, Weak bridge

00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:16.137
trust model, Small signer set; keys concentrated.

00:01:16.137 --> 00:01:20.454
Mango Markets, Oct 2022 (~$110M), Collateral price

00:01:20.454 --> 00:01:24.433
pumped on thin markets, then borrowed against,

00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:29.727
Oracle manipulation, Thin-market collateral valued at spot.

00:01:29.727 --> 00:01:34.418
FTX, Nov 2022, Exchange used customer funds, Custodial

00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:40.007
(CeFi) counterparty failure, Opaque reserves; "not your keys".

00:01:40.007 --> 00:01:45.867
Euler Finance, March 2023 (~$197M, later largely returned), Logic

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:50.395
flaw in a lending function, Contract bug missed by

00:01:50.395 --> 00:01:55.367
audits, Complex new function added after earlier audits.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.676
Curve pools, July 2023, Reentrancy guard broken

00:02:00.676 --> 00:02:04.317
by a compiler bug, Toolchain risk, Rare.

00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:06.757
Shows audited code can fail from below.

00:02:08.057 --> 00:02:10.572
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:02:10.572 --> 00:02:13.871
Using the table: a new stablecoin offers 18%

00:02:13.871 --> 00:02:18.277
"sustainable" yield, backed by its own governance token.

00:02:18.277 --> 00:02:21.408
That's the UST pattern: reflexive collateral and

00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:23.817
yield with no matching cash flow.

00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:25.292
Rating: High.

00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:26.557
Verdict: don't hold.

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:29.317
Here's your checklist.

00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:30.852
Do it now, for real.

00:02:30.852 --> 00:02:33.033
First, for every position, I've asked

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.341
which failure pattern it resembles.

00:02:35.341 --> 00:02:39.936
And finally, My register (8.2) includes these seven patterns.

00:02:41.236 --> 00:02:42.446
Question 1.

00:02:42.446 --> 00:02:44.471
What pattern did Mango Markets show?

00:02:48.891 --> 00:02:52.546
The answer: Oracle manipulation of thin-market collateral.

00:02:53.846 --> 00:02:55.091
Question 2.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:57.096
What did FTX show DeFi users?

00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:04.443
The answer: Custodial counterparty risk: "not

00:03:04.443 --> 00:03:06.161
your keys, not your coins".

00:03:07.461 --> 00:03:08.731
Question 3.

00:03:08.731 --> 00:03:10.406
UST's main warning sign?

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:17.763
The answer: High yield with no matching real

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.766
cash flow, backed by a reflexive sister token.

00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:24.581
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:24.581 --> 00:03:27.126
Next up, Lesson 6.6: Vote-escrow

00:03:27.126 --> 00:03:30.366
tokenomics, bribes and governance markets.
